    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0311" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg241"/>

                <head>Lord Lyons to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1861-12-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 16, 1861.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have this afternoon had the honor to
                    receive two notes from you dated thirteen days ago, and a third dated twelve
                    days ago. They relate to the representations which I felt it to be my duty to
                    address to you with regard to the <pb facs="0312" n="242" xml:id="pg242"/>
                    treatment to which seamen belonging to the British schooners Revere and Louisa
                    Agnes were subjected by officers of the United States navy. It is not my
                    purpose, on the present occasion, to make any observations on their contents. I
                    hasten, however, to inform you that they have only reached me to-day, lest I
                    should be deemed guilty of discourtesy in not having acknowledged the receipt of
                    them until so long after their dates.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient, humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>LYONS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
